## Database Entry Structure (per capital)
Each capital in the database gets its own Quire entry page. Create a subdirectory for each institution. Use Quire's object entry type with a consistent tombstone structure. See quire doc and quire documentation for more info. 

## Suggested Initial Database Entries
Begin with capitals for which good photographic and provenance documentation exists. Expand as the project develops. Suggested initial entries:
▸	Meadows Museum, SMU, Dallas (MM.96.01) — the primary object of study (already documented in Section 3)
▸	Museo Arqueológico Nacional, Madrid — Bugella Altamirano (2018) documents several Cordoban Islamic capitals in this collection
▸	Conjunto Arqueológico de Medina Azahara, Córdoba — in-situ or excavated capitals held at the site museum
